  VALUES
    ('ios_crash_gate', 'iOS crash gate', 'blocked', 'Authenticated App Store Connect confirms one iOS 1.0.1 crash on 2026-08-25, but privacy suppression exposes no device, OS, crash report, stack, or UUID. Product commit ee7c36f retains the reachable-path hardening and adds a strict Apple Empty/Fresh/Stale surface contract with 18 passing XCTest cases plus successful app/widget/watch Release simulator builds. Those preventive results cannot be attributed to the historical event and do not replace symbolication, physical iPhone QA, or post-rollout evidence.', 'Obtain any diagnostic report Apple later exposes, symbolicate if available, run exact signed physical iPhone QA, and collect post-rollout evidence'),
    ('open_meteo_promotion_clearance', 'Open-Meteo promotion clearance', 'pending', 'The authenticated Gmail thread and broad Open-Meteo searches were checked read-only at 2026-08-29 13:12 +05:00. The clarification sent to info@open-meteo.com at 06:05:07 remains the only indexed matching message and has label SENT; no inbound Open-Meteo reply is indexed in this account. This does not prove delivery or cover another account or a future/unindexed reply. Written clearance remains absent.', 'Monitor the sent thread and record an unambiguous written response'),
    ('release_artifact_source_sync', 'Release artifact source sync', 'blocked', 'Product commit ee7c36f resolves to Android phone 1.1.0 (8), Wear OS 1.1.0 (1000008), and Apple 1.1.0 (6). Phone AAB SHA-256 e16da522aca84776419a999db82a9ddb5a42b15660516bfe6f1fd65cf5a3edcb and mapping SHA-256 7e678576d95e36dd8e27cab78a565a47a1539a3caf6f769a283f9aca415a324f pass Bundletool 1.18.3 and embedded-VCS checks but the AAB has 0 signature entries. Wear AAB SHA-256 d1088ec635b69258baf5aaa42e42423b930a97a3077f059a2ae59c6d06061e71 embeds ee7c36f and has 0 signature entries; the retained signed Wear AAB embeds historical revision 4d9492a. Apple simulator hashes are app 279185d6778c7819d889a1f769d8ce2eb10b861790ed4ef2cc833044946aad90, widget bd651c05eb19551853fd5dde604fafdc7233f1615f21a9462b20f45199dc3209, and watch 14c419fb71f35097c0fe4396183acb1d701ef229ea55f3608a2982d5bab5c493; UUID-matched dSYMs verify, but these are ad-hoc simulator products, not archives. Android protected lookup and Apple private-key use remain unavailable. There is no exact-current signed phone/Wear artifact, distribution-signed Apple archive, or signed-artifact physical matrix.', 'Restore private signing authorization without replacing the existing identities, then create exact-current signed phone vc8, Wear 1000008, and Apple build-6 artifacts, verify identities and hashes, and record exact physical QA'),
    ('android_physical_smoke', 'Android device smoke', 'blocked', 'Historical exact commit df5f824 debug APK SHA-256 fb039c02964a0cbd49d9702998a2cba967c63bbc9ff368bcda9ea44936f0c753 passed fresh-install physical API 25 QA and a same-certificate preserved-data update on the physical API 36 Samsung; pulled bytes matched on both. Product commit ee7c36f adds fail-closed widget/Wear freshness behavior and has API 24 phone-widget plus API 37 round-Wear emulator coverage, but no source-synced signed physical tablet, widget, or paired Wear OS result. The current physical gate therefore remains blocked.', 'Sign and verify phone vc8, then run the exact signed artifact on phone and tablet plus widget and paired Wear OS paths'),
    ('ios_physical_smoke', 'iOS physical smoke', 'blocked', 'Product commit ee7c36f Apple 1.1.0 (6) Release simulator executable hashes are app 279185d6778c7819d889a1f769d8ce2eb10b861790ed4ef2cc833044946aad90, widget bd651c05eb19551853fd5dde604fafdc7233f1615f21a9462b20f45199dc3209, and watch 14c419fb71f35097c0fe4396183acb1d701ef229ea55f3608a2982d5bab5c493. UUID-matched dSYMs and 18 surface XCTest cases pass, but all three products are simulator-only with ad-hoc linker signatures, no TeamIdentifier, no archive, and no upload eligibility. The iPad CoreDevice/DDI path is usable, but no exact-current signed build exists; iPhone, iPad, WidgetKit, and paired-watch physical coverage remains required.', 'Create and verify distribution-signed build 6, then run the exact artifact on iPhone and the now-usable iPad CoreDevice path plus widget and paired watch paths'),
    ('domain_activation', 'Domain activation', 'pass', 'At 2026-08-29 10:40–10:41 +05:00, authenticated GitHub Pages settings showed DNS check successful and Enforce HTTPS enabled. The Let''s Encrypt certificate has CN nimbo.uz, SANs nimbo.uz/www.nimbo.uz, and validates for both hosts. WHOIS, .uz delegation, authoritative Cloudflare records, and independent 1.1.1.1/8.8.8.8 resolution pass. HTTPS returns 200 with verification result 0 for all 12 published UZ-root/RU/EN landing, press, privacy, and support routes plus growth, robots, sitemap, and the valid metadata schema. HTTP apex redirects to HTTPS; HTTP www reaches HTTPS apex in two redirects; HTTPS www redirects directly to HTTPS apex. All 12 localized HTML routes have the expected HTTPS canonical and language. Uzbek intentionally uses ' || chr(47) || ' rather than a separate ' || chr(47) || 'uz' || chr(47) || ' route.', 'Maintain dated DNS, certificate, redirect, canonical, and localized-route verification at each release'),
    ('store_policy_console_clearance', 'Store policy console clearance', 'pass', 'The 2026-08-28 App Store read-only check found no open review/compliance action. Google Play reported no policy issues at 2026-08-29 13:12 +05:00; production remained active at 1.0.2 (6), 100%. At 13:59:40 +05:00, UZ Custom Store Listing 4834799756935529888 was saved only as Draft, not submitted for review or published; Publishing overview still showed the latest publication on 2026-08-27. This is point-in-time Console evidence, not a guarantee against later review. See growth/quality/store-policy-console-2026-08-28.md and growth/quality/google-play-console-2026-08-29.md.', 'Re-check both app-global store policy surfaces at the next evidence cutoff')
